<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/20th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · War</p><h1 class="enc-title">Paquisha War</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1981</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Paquisha War was a brief armed conflict between Ecuador and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peru">Peru</a> in January and February 1981 in the Cordillera del Cóndor, in a border area left undemarcated by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rio-protocol">Rio de Janeiro Protocol</a>. Peruvian forces expelled Ecuadorian troops from outposts that Ecuador had named after the settlement of Paquisha. The guarantor states arranged a ceasefire, but the dispute remained unresolved until 1998.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/paquisha-war.jpg" alt="Paquisha War" width="320" height="404" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: The University of Texas at Austin · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Cenepa_river_basin_Paquisha_war.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
